+# Agentic iterative development -- cycle protocol v1
+
+## Input
+Every development agent receives the **same complete RC14.6 ZIP**, its own short dispatch prompt, and the agent-specific instruction already packaged in `agent_cycle/Axx.md`. The user attaches no other files unless a specifically authorized input is needed. The historical A01..A09 assignments are provenance, NOT ownership for this cycle.
+
+## Dispatch
+Use eight separate sessions with **unchanged** full baseline. Agents A10..A17 may work in parallel because edited paths are exclusive. Agent A99 receives the original full ZIP and **all eight** delta ZIPs, and does NOT start before all eight are present. An agent's delivery is just its delta ZIP. The original full package must not be rebuilt independently by parallel agents.
+
+## Validated delta envelope
+`tools/agent_cycle.py delta BASE WORK A10 A10-delta.zip` packages only changed/new/deleted paths authorized by `agent_cycle/assignments.json`, and SHA-256 preimages and new contents. The tool checks source manifest provenance, symlinks, frozen files, duplicate/malicious ZIP names and a 32 MiB delta maximum. Test evidence under `agent_cycle/deliveries/Axx/` is owned by the agent; each source modification must have accompanying evidence, but missing native runtimes are honestly BLOCKED. The integrator must verify hashes and reject invalid inputs, not patch them quietly.
+
+## Integration, testing, delivery
+A99 verifies and merges exactly eight provenance-bound deltas. Integration conflicts and scientific blockers are identified before release qualification. A99 may perform explicitly recorded harmonization, with full regression results, all actual tool versions and limitations. A99 must regenerate current source inventory and wheel, never touch the historical foundation lock or silently change contracts. No unqualified fabrication claim.
+
+## One-click user feedback
+Each integrated release ships `qualification_plan.json`. In the desktop launcher, `Qualify this laptop` has **one** action: run fixed release test. It writes `qualification-reports/SQE-RC14_6-report-0001.zip`, 0002, etc, automatically. `CYCLE.json` contains baseline, plan digest, previous hash-verified feedback metadata and future-agent blocker hints. Private user projects are never copied. For subsequent releases the series prefix changes, maintaining prior ZIPs if deliberately retained in the folder. Reports may compare outcomes, but native results must rerun unless a **separately approved exact-cache protocol** establishes identical geometry/solver/tool versions/material boundaries and does not relabel old output as new results.
+
+## Next cycle
+After receiving the user report, classify FAIL, BLOCKED and non-converged native evidence, identify dependencies, update tasks and owners, package full new baseline, repeat parallel delta/one-click loop. Never reinterpret missing tools as PASS.
